answers.body:
No, what you are doing is not valid according to the OpenMP specification (OpenMP version 3.1, §2.5 Worksharing Constructs): Restrictions : The following restrictions apply to worksharing constructs: Each worksharing region must be encountered by all threads in a team or by none at all. (emphasis mine) This changes a bit in OpenMP 4.0 with the introduction of cancellation points, but the general idea remains the same. But since you are using schedule(dynamic) which defaults to a chunk size of one iteration, you can use explicit tasks instead: #pragma omp parallel sections
{
   #pragma omp section
   {
      printf("This is a single thread doing something\n");
   }
   #pragma omp section
   {
      for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++)
      {
         #pragma omp task
         {
            int thread_id = omp_get_thread_num();
            printf("%d-th hello from thread %d\n", i, thread_id);
         }
      }
   }
} You could also implement your own sections like you've done in your original code and you could also reimplement static scheduling (if necessary) by using the thread IDs to compute the iteration range.

